### Important Notice

The Software is **source-available, not open source**. Being able to see the source does not mean you may modify it, give it to anyone, use it commercially, train models on it, or restate its rules. **Everything other than what Sections 3 and 4 expressly allow is prohibited.** Read this License in full before you download, install, run, or let an AI agent read the Software. Pay special attention to Section 5 (Prohibited Acts), Section 12 (Termination), Section 13 (Remedies), Sections 14–15 (No Warranty; Limitation of Liability) and Section 19 (Governing Law and Disputes).

### Section 1 Definitions

1.1 **Licensor**: 叶子 (Yezi; GitHub: YEZI-Studio; legal name in Section 21), the person offering the Software under this License.

1.2 **Software**: everything the Licensor makes available under this License, in any form or medium, including source code, compiled modules, executables, scripts, configuration, prompts and prompt templates, task templates, schemas, documentation, images and data, and any part, update, patch or later version of them; it also includes content the Licensor provides to you through an online service (for example a license check or a rules relay). The Software is named YEZI-VE (Visual Elevation).

1.3 **Protected Materials**: the rules and method content of the Software, including without limitation: HANDBOOK and other manuals (except the user-facing installation and run instructions in SKILL.md, which you may explain to yourself or your AI Agent; SKILL.md is still part of the Software and Section 5.2 applies to it); the rule tree, root rules, type cards, catalog card, series cards and check lists; prompts, prompt templates and task templates; schemas; gates and their thresholds, scoring anchors, reference frames, ruler images, calibration data and calibrated values; the orchestration flow, stage design, round limits and stop conditions; algorithms, measurement methods and their parameters. They remain Protected Materials in any form, whether verbatim, excerpted, translated, rewritten, summarized, screenshotted, screen-recorded, spoken, charted, restated by an AI, or otherwise. Stage numbers and names, round limits, stop conditions, thresholds, scores and their anchors that appear in SKILL.md, in reports (report.md) or in messages the Software shows while running remain Protected Materials: you may follow and view them, but may not compile them separately, publish them, or use them for anything Section 5 prohibits.

1.4 **Run Artifacts**: every file and piece of data the Software generates while running, other than the Final Video, including without limitation each episode's task files (TASK.md), context files (ctx/), model call records (calls/), topic and director files, beat maps, shot lists, gate results, the rule ledger (gates_tree.json), reports, logs, shot code, request files, the engine copy the Software places in each episode directory, render parameters, caches and intermediate videos. Run Artifacts contain or reflect Protected Materials and are part of the Software.

1.5 **Final Video**: the final video file the Software generates for you (normally under an episode's deliver/ directory; film/with_audio.mp4 if the delivery gate did not pass), and any transcode, compression or crop you make of it for your own viewing or for publication under Section 4.

1.6 **Personal Non-Commercial Use**: use by one natural person for his or her own private purposes, such as personal study, hobby, private entertainment or private sharing with family and friends, with no commercial application anticipated at the time of use or afterwards.

1.7 **Commercial Use**: any use intended, directly or indirectly, to obtain monetary benefit or commercial advantage, whether or not any income is actually received. Every case listed in Section 5.3 is Commercial Use, but Commercial Use is not limited to those cases.

1.8 **Derivative Work**: any modification, adaptation, translation, port, rewrite, reorganization, extension, remix or other new work based on the Software or the Protected Materials, including a functionally equivalent re-implementation.

1.9 **AI Agent**: any artificial-intelligence model, agent, automation script or tool that reads, runs, analyzes or generates content on instruction, such as Claude, Codex, DeepSeek and other large language models and coding agents.

1.10 **You**: the natural person who accepts this License.

1.11 **Organization**: any company, sole proprietorship, partnership, studio, MCN agency, school, training institution, association, non-profit, government body or other organization.

1.12 **Technical Protection Measures**: any technical means the Licensor uses to control access to or use of the Software or to protect the Protected Materials, such as license checks, device binding, signature checks, compilation, obfuscation, encryption and online-service authentication.

1.13 **Competing Product**: any product, service, tool, rule set, template, course or model that has the same or similar functions as the Software or could substitute for it, whether paid or free.

1.14 **Third-Party Materials**: components, fonts, music, footage, software and services that do not belong to the Licensor and are provided by third parties under their own terms; see NOTICE.md.

1.15 **Official Channel**: https://github.com/YEZI-Studio/YEZI-VE (the Licensor's official repository on GitHub).

### Section 2 Acceptance

2.1 In order to get any license under these terms, you must agree to all of them as both strict obligations and conditions to all your licenses.

2.2 From the version that adds a first-run confirmation onward, when the Software runs for the first time it shows the key terms of this License and asks you to expressly click or type 「同意」 ("I agree"); you may not run the Software until you have done so. You must give that agreement personally; no AI Agent, script or other person may click or type it for you. In addition, by downloading, installing, copying, running or reading the Software, or by instructing an AI Agent to do any of these, you agree to this License. If you do not agree, do none of these things.

