### Section 3 The Only Permitted Use (License Grant)

3.1 As long as you keep complying with every term of this License, the Licensor grants you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, revocable, limited license **only** to:

(a) obtain the Software from the Official Channel and install it on no more than 2 physical devices that you personally own and actually control and that only you use (each virtual machine, container, system image or clone counts as a separate device and is subject to Section 5.15);

(b) run the Software **unmodified**, in the way SKILL.md and the accompanying documentation describe (including through an AI Agent), to generate Final Videos for yourself. By design the Software has AI Agents generate shot code, context files (ctx/), task files and request files in each episode directory, and copies its engine there; these are Run Artifacts and are not modifications, plugins or Derivative Works under Section 5.1, but they may be used only by the Software within that episode's run and its resumptions;

(c) for the purpose of running the Software, let it send what it needs (including prompts, rule excerpts, task files and Run Artifacts) to model services or tools that you choose and are responsible for (for example the DeepSeek API, Codex, Claude Code), and read on your device the files needed to run it. Where such a service offers an option such as "do not use my data to train or improve models", you must choose not to allow it. **Safe harbor:** provided you have made that choice (no choice is needed where the service offers none), what the Software sends under this item, and what that service does with it under its own terms (including retention, review and training), does not put you in breach of Sections 4.4, 5.5, 5.6, 5.7 or 5.16 and does not end this License. The safe harbor covers only what the Software sends in order to run; it does not cover anything you send, paste or upload separately;

(d) adjust a run only in the ways SKILL.md lists: command-line arguments, environment variables, per-episode input files (for example inputs/music.json and notes files), and configuration items SKILL.md expressly says users may change. Such adjustments are not modifications of the Software;

(e) keep one backup copy, which is also subject to this License and counts toward the device limit in Section 3.1(a);

(f) let the AI Agent you use to run the Software under Section 3.1(b) read Run Artifacts and report the results of that run to you personally (for example the Final Video's path, the report's conclusions about that episode, progress, logs, errors and why it stopped). Such reports are for you alone and limited to what is needed to explain that run's results; what the AI Agent reads for this purpose is treated under Section 3.1(c). Reporting to you under this item is not a breach of Section 5.6, but it may not be used to compile, export or reconstruct Protected Materials.

3.2 Every item in Section 3.1 must also be Personal Non-Commercial Use.

3.3 **Except as expressly allowed in this Section and Section 4, the Licensor grants you no other right; anything this License does not expressly allow is prohibited.**

### Section 4 Use of Final Videos

4.1 While you comply with this License, you may:

(a) keep and watch your Final Videos;

(b) send them privately to family and friends;

(c) publish them on personal social-media accounts in your own name, provided that the Final Video itself generates no direct or indirect income (no ad revenue, no creator-incentive or revenue-share programs, no tips, no product sales, no sponsored or brand content, no soft ads, and no funneling to any paid product or service). If a platform does not let you exclude the Final Video from monetization, do not publish it there without the Licensor's written permission.

4.2 When you publish a Final Video you must:

(a) comply with the terms of the Third-Party Materials in it, including posting the required music credit in the description (for example the exact NCS credit text) and crediting authors of footage licensed under CC BY (see NOTICE.md and each episode's report);

(b) not state or imply that the Licensor made it, that it is part of the Licensor's works or series (for example CHROMA), or that the Licensor endorses it; and not use the Licensor's name, nickname (including 叶子 and its pinyin yezi / YEZI), brand (including YEZI-Studio), series names or the Software's name (YEZI-VE) as the name of the video or of your own series;

(c) optionally (not required) add a factual line such as "Made with YEZI-VE".

4.3 You may not, with respect to Final Videos:

(a) make any Commercial Use of them (including every case in Section 5.3);

(b) use them for any training or data purpose prohibited by Section 5.5;

(c) sell, rent, license or distribute them as stock, templates, samples or asset packs;

(d) use them for any unlawful or harmful purpose prohibited by Section 5.13.

4.4 Run Artifacts may be kept only on the devices where you installed the Software under Section 3.1(a), for your own viewing. You may not disclose, show or distribute them to anyone, except to the Licensor when reporting a problem, what the Software itself sends to the model services or tools you choose in order to run under Section 3.1(c), and reports your AI Agent gives you under Section 3.1(f).

4.5 The Licensor does not claim copyright in the Final Video itself, but this does not expand any of your rights in the Software or the Protected Materials, nor change who owns Third-Party Materials. Third-Party Materials in a Final Video still belong to their owners, and you are responsible for using them lawfully.

4.6 After this License ends you may not publish any new Final Video; if it ended because of your breach, you must take down Final Videos published in breach when the Licensor asks.

### Section 5 Prohibited Acts

Except as Sections 3 and 4 expressly allow, you may not do any of the following, yourself or through anyone else or any AI Agent:

5.1 **Modification and derivatives.** Modify, adapt, translate, port (for example to another language, framework, render engine, model or platform), rewrite, patch, extend or remix the Software or the Protected Materials, or make any Derivative Work, including plugins, hooks or wrappers that change the Software's behavior and any functionally equivalent re-implementation.

5.2 **Distribution, resale, hosting and bundling.** Copy the Software or any part of it for others, redistribute, sell, resell, rent, lend, sublicense or transfer it; upload it to any code host, cloud drive, group chat, forum, mirror or model hub; host it as an online service, API, bot, done-for-you platform or in any other form for others to use; package, bundle or integrate it into any other product, template, asset pack, toolkit, course or service; or share one installation among several people.

5.3 **Commercial Use.** Make any Commercial Use of the Software, the Protected Materials, Run Artifacts or Final Videos, including without limitation:
(a) making videos for clients, employers or any third party, including free trials, pitches and samples (Section 5.14 separately prohibits this whether or not it is paid or commercial);
(b) taking orders, doing work for hire, outsourcing or crowdsourcing, or using it while providing any paid service;
(c) ad revenue, creator-incentive programs, revenue sharing, tips, product sales, sponsored deals, brand partnerships, soft ads or any kind of promotion;
(d) use on company, shop, brand or institutional accounts;
(e) paid teaching, courses, bootcamps, paid communities, paid knowledge products, consulting, coaching or any paid training;
(f) as a giveaway, selling point or add-on of any paid product;
(g) fundraising, pitches, business proposals or bids;
